Foundation — corporate scholarships</p><p class=\"text-xs font-mono text-gray-500\">vidyasaarathi.co.in</p></div><div class=\"border rounded-xl p-4 border-orange-200 bg-orange-50\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-2\"><span class=\"text-xs font-bold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-white/70 text-orange-700\">Technical</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-globe w-4 h-4 text-orange-700 opacity-60\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0-20\"></path><path d=\"M2 12h20\"></path></svg></div><h3 class=\"font-bold text-sm text-orange-700 mb-1\">AICTE Scholarships</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-gray-600 mb-2\">PG GATE stipend &amp; technical scholarships</p><p class=\"text-xs font-mono text-gray-500\">aicte-india.org</p></div><div class=\"border rounded-xl p-4 border-teal-200 bg-teal-50\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-2\"><span class=\"text-xs font-bold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-white/70 text-teal-700\">Science</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-globe w-4 h-4 text-teal-700 opacity-60\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0-20\"></path><path d=\"M2 12h20\"></path></svg></div><h3 class=\"font-bold text-sm text-teal-700 mb-1\">INSPIRE — DST</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-gray-600 mb-2\">Science scholarship for top 1% students</p><p class=\"text-xs font-mono text-gray-500\">online-inspire.gov.in</p></div><div class=\"border rounded-xl p-4 border-indigo-200 bg-indigo-50\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-2\"><span class=\"text-xs font-bold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-white/70 text-indigo-700\">International</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-globe w-4 h-4 text-indigo-700 opacity-60\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0-20\"></path><path d=\"M2 12h20\"></path></svg></div><h3 class=\"font-bold text-sm text-indigo-700 mb-1\">DAAD India</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-gray-600 mb-2\">Germany scholarships for Masters &amp; PhD</p><p class=\"text-xs font-mono text-gray-500\">daad.in</p></div></div></div><div class=\"mt-8 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-5\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class=\"space-y-4\"><details class=\"group border border-gray-100 rounded-xl overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-sm text-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-50 list-none\">Can I apply for multiple scholarships simultaneously?<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-4 h-4 text-gray-400 group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-3\">Yes, you can apply for multiple scholarships. However, some government schemes restrict you from receiving more than one Central Government scholarship at the same time. Private scholarships generally have no such restriction. Always read the terms carefully.</div></details><details class=\"group border border-gray-100 rounded-xl overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-sm text-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-50 list-none\">What documents are most commonly required?<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-4 h-4 text-gray-400 group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-3\">Almost every scholarship requires: Aadhaar card, income certificate from competent authority, previous exam marksheet, current admission and fee receipt, bank account details (linked with Aadhaar for DBT), and passport size photograph. Keep digital and physical copies ready.</div></details><details class=\"group border border-gray-100 rounded-xl overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-sm text-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-50 list-none\">What is the NSP (National Scholarship Portal)?<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-4 h-4 text-gray-400 group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-3\">The National Scholarship Portal (scholarships.gov.in) is the official Government of India portal that hosts 50+ central government scholarship schemes. A single registration gives you access to multiple schemes. All central government scholarships are now disbursed through Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) via NSP.</div></details><details class=\"group border border-gray-100 rounded-xl overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-sm text-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-50 list-none\">How do I get income certificate for scholarship?<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-4 h-4 text-gray-400 group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-3\">Income certificate is issued by the Tehsildar/SDM/Circle Officer in your district. Visit your local government office with proof of family income (salary slips, ITR, or declaration). It typically takes 7–15 working days. Some states issue it online through their e-district portals.</div></details><details class=\"group border border-gray-100 rounded-xl overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-sm text-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-50 list-none\">When should I start applying for scholarships?<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-4 h-4 text-gray-400 group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-3\">Start applying as soon as you get your admission letter. Most scholarship deadlines fall between August–November. Government portals typically open in July-August. P